    "source_description_html": "An <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MRE\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:MRE\">MRE</a> contains a complete meal for use in the field. This was given out by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_National_Guard\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:United States National Guard\">United States National Guard</a> after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Rita\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Hurricane Rita\">Hurricane Rita</a>. Menu #10 \n<ul><li>Chili and <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Macaroni\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Macaroni\">Macaroni</a></li>\n<li>Wheat snack bread</li>\n<li>Molasses cookie</li>\n<li>Cheese spread with jalapenos</li>\n<li>Tootsie rolls</li>\n<li>salt</li>\n<li>sugar</li>\n<li>coco beverage powder</li>\n<li>ground coffee</li>\n<li>ground red pepper</li>\n<li>gum</li>\n<li><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Moist_towelette&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Moist towelette (page does not exist)\">moist towelette</a></li>\n<li>paper napkin</li>\n<li>matchbook</li>\n<li>spoon</li></ul>\nTaken next to the window on carpet, cropped in Adobe Photoshop. (Further post-processing is welcome if I don't get around to it.)",
